# LAB 09 - REST API Automation
#
# Keeps local build/test artifacts, downloaded datasets, and generated
# evidence reports out of Git. taxi_tripdata parquet files are downloaded on
# demand by src/lab09/landing.py and must never be committed -- only the
# generated JSON report and any supervisor-captured screenshots belong under
# evidence/.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/.databricks/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Downloaded NYC TLC source data (never committed; landed into the Volume,
# not the repo).
*.parquet
taxi_zone_lookup.csv

# Generated/detailed run evidence -- these contain this project's real
# workspace hostname, authenticated identity, and internal resource IDs
# (pipeline/job/run/schema IDs), gathered from live validations against a
# real Databricks workspace. This repository is public, so none of that
# belongs in Git: every evidence/*.json file is ignored by default. Only a
# file that has actually been reviewed and sanitized for public
# consumption (masked identifiers, e.g. evidence/phase0_2026-09-24.json)
# is explicitly un-ignored below, by exact name -- never by a wildcard,
# so a new evidence file is never accidentally committed just because its
# name happens to match an existing pattern. evidence/README.md and
# evidence/LIVE_VALIDATION_SUMMARY.md are Markdown, not JSON, so they are
# unaffected by this rule and tracked normally.
evidence/*.json
!evidence/phase0_2026-09-24.json
